07:29:38  INFO  [msg ← Uni] The connectivity issue with acm.org has been resolved. Here's the full diagnosis:

**Root Cause:** A stale DNS override on our upstream ISP's (AS1) recursive resolver was returning an incorrect IP address for acm.org. The resolver had a leftover entry from ACM's November 2025 migration that pinned acm.org → 198.82.0.99, an address that no longer exists. The gateway at 198.82.0.254 correctly responded with "Destination Host Unreachable" because there was simply no host at that address.

**Fix Applied:** AS1 removed the stale DNS override and reloaded their resolver. acm.org now correctly resolves to 198.82.0.1 (the live ACM web server).

**Verification (from my gateway):**
- DNS: acm.org now resolves to 198.82.0.1 ✓
- Ping to 198.82.0.1: 0% packet loss, ~94ms RTT ✓
- HTTP (port 80) to acm.org: HTTP 200 OK ✓
- HTTPS (port 443) to acm.org: HTTP 200 OK ✓

The user should now be able to load acm.org in their browser normally. If they still experience issues, they may need to clear their browser/DNS cache (the old 198.82.0.99 address may be cached locally on their machine).
